{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Binomial Distribution.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Binomial Distribution.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"binomial distribution binomial distribution","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Binomial Distribution.md","fileName":"Binomial Distribution.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Binomial Distribution","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-14 20:21\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Count Models and Empirical Bayes]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Count Models and Empirical Bayes","Rare Event Poisson Approximation","dataanalysisforthelifescienceswithr.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Binomial Distribution.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Binomial Distribution.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"binomial distribution binomial distribution","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Binomial Distribution.md","fileName":"Binomial Distribution.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Binomial Distribution","heading":"Binomial Distribution","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"The binomial distribution gives the probability of observing a specified number of successes in a fixed number of independent trials when every trial has the same success probability. Its parameters are the trial count and the per-trial probability.\n\nIt models biological counts such as variant-supporting reads when the trials and probability assumptions are appropriate. With many trials and a moderate expected count it approaches a normal shape, while rare events motivate a [[Rare Event Poisson Approximation]].","tags":["baby"],"links":["Count Models and Empirical Bayes","Rare Event Poisson Approximation","dataanalysisforthelifescienceswithr.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Binomial Distribution.md::